+# #41 R20 synthetic external control read-half fault
+
+Source candidate based on integration `7459e233fc58c03b49b8dc1a5204bfb348e074d5`. The four production C inputs match the R18 inputs byte for byte. The fixed broker, I/O and owner policy, and startup-74 source proof are read-only links to the R18 source packet. R20 uses a fresh stage, marker, generation, and installation.
+
+The fixture waits for the original guardian's exact running and natural `ROOT_EXIT <generation> 0 0` frames. FakeDispatcher holds its completion ACK until the fixture has filled the guardian's shared fd3 send queue and obtained positive, sub-1 MiB backpressure with EAGAIN. After FakeDispatcher writes the ACK, the fixture rechecks protection and calls `shutdown(SHUT_RD)` on its own control peer. It keeps the peer's write half, fake Dispatcher connection, and filler duplicate open.
+
+The observation journal records successful shutdown and repeated samples from the original pidfd that extend at least 250 ms after shutdown within the fixture's 5-second observation budget. Each sample requires the first observed fence bytes, a denied exclusive maintenance lock, and a nonterminal original guardian. The first fence bytes stay pinned through HOLD even when observation fails. A completed observation records `CONTROL_READ_HALF_FAULT_PROTECTION_HELD` and enters HOLD. A failed sample or syscall also enters HOLD. The observed EAGAIN belongs to the fixture duplicate. The guardian's exact errno, ACK consumption, and COMPLETE timing remain unobserved.
+
+A fresh literal Root challenge at HOLD can authorize the original pidfd signal once, following the retained R18 ownership checks. Expected disposition is guardian wait -9, genuine stdout/stderr EOF and reader joins for both original actors, original controller wait 2, and direct-child ECHILD in the controller and outer domains. The controller requires the same failed fence bytes after reap. When `SHUT_RD` was never attempted, it also requires the inherited bounded control EOF drain. When `SHUT_RD` returned or its outcome is uncertain, the controller records the shutdown state and excludes control EOF from the evidence. `MANUAL_DRAINED_NOT_PASS` is status 2. The separate fault observation receipt is required to establish that the planned injection and retention observations completed. Startup-74 remains the separate R18 failure path with status 3. Product admission remains blocked.
+
+## Commands for the new case
+
+The commands below use the existing R18 prepare, compiler, seal, and one-use runner workflow. Preparation follows source review. Compilation and artifact review bind the new configuration and executables. Run only with the fresh exact manifest clearance. Use the emitted literal commands in the original stdin for the before-START gate and the post-HOLD decision. The outer runner requires a TTY on stdin and exits 4 before opening the stage if stdin lacks one.
+
+```bash
+r20_packet=/workspace/work/mvp-implementation/recovery/r20-current-control-read-half-source
+r20_stage=/tmp/omp-external-control-read-half-r20-20261118
+r20_root=/workspace/work/omp-webui-current
+r20_marker=external-current-7459e23-control-read-half-r20
+
+# Pure source tests and pin check.
+cd "$r20_packet"
+/usr/bin/python3 -B -m unittest control_read_half_test -v
+sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
+
+# Later, after source review and preparation clearance.
+/usr/bin/python3 -B "$r20_packet/external_backpressure_stage.py" --prepare-source "$r20_marker"
+
+# Separate compiler window, using the same commands emitted in compiler-recipe.json.
+env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /usr/bin/gcc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -O2 -static \
+  "$r20_stage/root.c" -o "$r20_stage/release/bin/omp"
+env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /usr/bin/gcc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -O2 -static \
+  -include "$r20_stage/configuration.h" "$r20_root/compatibility/supervision/external-protector.c" \
+  -o "$r20_stage/release/bin/omp-external-protector"
+
+# Seal the unsigned artifacts for review.
+/usr/bin/python3 -B "$r20_packet/external_backpressure_stage.py" --seal-unsigned "$r20_marker"
+
+# Launch with tty: true in the execution tool and keep the original session stdin.
+# Substitute the literal SHA256 from the fresh exact-manifest Root clearance.
+cd "$r20_root"
+env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin HOME="$r20_stage/home" TMPDIR=/tmp LC_ALL=C \
+  /usr/bin/python3 -B "$r20_packet/external_backpressure.py" --run-once \
+  "$r20_marker" APPROVED_LITERAL_MANIFEST_SHA256
+```
